(Microbiota-based interventions for treatment-resistant bipolar depression: study protocol) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Rationale: Emerging evidence links dysbiosis to mood disorders. This pilot trial will) Tj
T*
(examine whether targeted microbiota manipulation can enhance standard psychiatric care in) Tj
T*
(treatment-refractory bipolar depression. Methods: Adults with confirmed bipolar disorder) Tj
T*
(\(I or II\) presenting with moderate-to-severe depressive symptoms despite ongoing) Tj
T*
(medication will be enrolled \(n=35\). Eligible participants must be on stable psychiatric) Tj
T*
(medication for >=4 weeks. Participants will be randomly allocated \(1:1\) to receive either) Tj
T*
(donor-sourced microbiota transplantation or self-microbiota transplantation \(autologous\),) Tj
T*
(delivered via colonoscopy. Both groups will continue usual psychiatric treatment.) Tj
T*
(Blinding: evaluators and participants will be masked to treatment allocation; microbiota) Tj
T*
(composition will be characterized using sequencing. Follow-up assessments occur weekly for) Tj
T*
(the first month, then monthly through week 24. Primary outcome: depressive symptom) Tj
T*
(severity assessed via validated depression rating scale. Secondary: anxiety, functional) Tj
T*
(capacity, tolerability, and microbiota diversity changes. Study design: double-blind,) Tj
T*
(parallel-arm pilot randomized controlled trial.) Tj
ET
